// A CUE WITH A FLAG AND A DOT — the texture the corpus had never written.
//
// test/cue-notes and test/cue-accidentals write quarters and chords: no cue in the tracked
// corpus carries a FLAG or a DOT, so when session 313 found that DrawNote drew a reduced
// flag and a reduced dot out of the STAFF's design instead of the cue's own, and fixed it,
// not one snapshot moved. This book is the observer for that pair and for the dot column
// above it (test/dotted-flag-dot-column is its full-size twin).
//
// MEASURED on LilyPond 2.26.0 (scratch/p314/cuedot-dump.ly — a CueVoice, whose
// ly/engraver-init.ly \name CueVoice sets fontSize = #-4; each number is the dot's LEFT
// minus its own head's LEFT, with the full-size answer from flagdot-dump.ly beside it):
//   cue g'8.   head ON A LINE, dot lifted   1.5431   (full size 2.5174)
//   cue f'8.   head IN A SPACE              1.0867   (full size 1.7542)
//   cue g'16.  head ON A LINE               1.5431   (full size 2.5174)
//   cue f'16.  head IN A SPACE              1.5431   (full size 2.5174)
// where 1.5431 = 0.7504 (the up stem's centre) + 0.5213 (the flag's own right) + 0.2714 (one
// dot width) and 1.0867 = 0.8154 (the head's ink right) + 0.2714. The SHAPE is the full-size
// one — three of the four stand right of the flag — and every term is the CUE font's own,
// which is not the staff's shrunk: LilyPond's cue head inks 0.8154 where the twenty's box at
// magstep(-4) would be 0.8215 (Emmentaler is optically sized; Design13's black head is
// 1.294282 against the twenty's 1.304200).
//
// ⚠️ THAT 0.006142 WAS LILY#'s UNTIL THIS FIXTURE EXISTED. DrawNote read the notehead's ink
// right and its stem attachment out of Design20 and multiplied by magstep, so the cue's dot
// column and its stem stood 0.006142 right of LilyPond's — and the GRACE half of the same
// island (0.004150, Design14) had been live ink since HANDOFF §2 U8 ⒝2 handed grace stems to
// this method. Both ask GrobFontSize.FontOf now, which is what the flag and the dot width
// beside them already did.
//
// The rests are BEAM BREAKERS: a beamed column has no flag, and then there is nothing to
// measure (scratch/p314/dots.lys made exactly that mistake).
octave absolute
time 4/4

part v { }

section A {
  v {
    cue { g8. r16 f8. r16 } r2 |
    cue { g16. r32 f16. r32 } r2 r4 |
  }
}

form main { ~A }

score main { staff ~v }
